  "configuration_id": "config_019",
  "reason": "The current best (config_018, acc=0.619) uses concat fusion in a multimodal multiprofile setup with avgpool aggregation. We have only tested concat fusion across all multimodal experiments, so the fusion strategy remains a major untested design axis. Config_019 is a controlled A/B test against config_018, changing only fusion from concat to weighted while holding all other factors (pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, multiprofile) constant. This directly answers whether the two modalities benefit from learned weighting versus simple concatenation. Given that RNA dominates (0.485 vs ~0.21 for image), a weighted scheme could down-weight the weaker image signal and sharpen the RNA contribution, potentially yielding a meaningful gain. If it does not improve, we cleanly rule out fusion as a lever and redirect budget toward encoder upgrades (scvi/scgpt or ViT-L). Under a limited budget, this single-variable comparison to the current best is the highest-information, lowest-risk next step."
}

